exports[`shipped marketing route composition security retains its rendered sections, links and visuals 1`] = `
{
  "glyphs": [],
  "headings": [
    "Secure by construction.Agents reach your tools only through gates you control.",
    "Four guarantees. They hold whoever runs the agent.",
    "Its own computerEvery session runs isolated.",
    "Its own identityAn agent never borrows your role.",
    "Logins stay outConnector logins never enter the computer.",
    "Checked and recordedRules first, then the audit log.",
    "How it works.One layer at a time.",
    "Identity and roles",
    "Agent permissions",
    "The computer and egress",
    "Connectors and approvals",
    "Secrets",
    "Models",
    "Changes and review",
    "Identity and roles",
    "What enforces each rule. All but one run outside the computer.",
    "Run it where your policy says.And read every line of what you run.",
    "Kortix Cloud",
    "Self-hosted",
    "Your VPC or on-prem",
    "Open source",
    "SAML 2.0 and SCIM 2.0",
    "Any model",
    "Security questions.Answered from the code.",
  ],
  "links": [
    [
      "Talk to us",
      "/contact",
    ],
    [
      "Read the security docs",
      "/docs/guide#security",
    ],
    [
      "Bring us your review",
      "/contact",
    ],
    [
      "write to the team",
      "/contact",
    ],
  ],
  "sections": [
    "hero",
    "pillars",
    "how-it-works",
    "enforcement",
    "trust",
    "faq",
  ],
  "securityContent": "Secure by construction.Agents reach your tools only through gates you control.A person grants an agent access. The agent runs as itself on its own isolated computer. Kortix decides which keys reach that computer, and checks every app call, model call and change it makes.Talk to usRead the security docsA personYouChoose which agent may run, and grant it access.Its own computerThe agentActs as itself, never with your role.Run a commandKortix gateTool rulesChecked by the runtime, before the tool runs.ResourceFiles and commandsReached only after the check.1Tool rules2Connector broker3Secret broker4LLM gateway5ReviewThe runtime checks allow, ask or deny before every tool runs.One computer per session. Connector logins and Kortix’s model keys never enter it.Four guarantees. They hold whoever runs the agent.Its own computerEvery session runs isolated.One cloud computer per sessionIts own branch of the repositoryNothing shared with another sessionIts own identityAn agent never borrows your role.Grants are deny-by-defaultIt cannot grant itself moreYou choose who may run itLogins stay outConnector logins never enter the computer.Kortix makes each app callSecrets encrypted per projectEnforced secrets swapped outsideChecked and recordedRules first, then the audit log.Allow, Ask or Block per actionOne approval per exact callEvery action on recordHow it works.One layer at a time.Identity and rolesWho may open a project, and which agents they may run.Agent permissionsAn agent acts as itself, with only what you grant.The computer and egressEach session gets its own isolated cloud computer.Connectors and approvalsKortix holds the login and decides each call.SecretsEncrypted per project, delivered only where allowed.ModelsEvery model request passes one gateway.Changes and reviewWork reaches main through a change request.Identity and rolesPeople sign in with SAML single sign-on, or a password with two-factor.Each person holds an account role and a role in each project. Groups grant a project to many people at once.Account roleOwnerAdminMemberProject roleManagerMemberSign-inSAML 2.0 SSOSCIM 2.0Two-factorSession timeoutWhat enforces each rule. All but one run outside the computer.What enforces each rule.RuleEnforced byOn denyA valid credentialKortix API401A role that allows the actionKortix API, IAM403, or 404 if hiddenThe agent’s own permissionsKortix API, IAM403No self-granted permissionsKortix API, IAM403 agent_grant_escalationTool, command and path rulesRuntime, inside the computerAsk waits, deny refusesConnector rulesConnector broker202 held, 403 deniedNo connector calls to private addressesConnector brokerconnector_egress_blockedEnforced secret, listed hosts onlySecret brokerNot swappedPush only to its own branchKortix git403Merge needs project.gitops.mergeKortix API403 CR_SELF_MERGE_REFUSEDA valid credentialKortix API401A role that allows the actionKortix API, IAM403, or 404 if hiddenThe agent’s own permissionsKortix API, IAM403No self-granted permissionsKortix API, IAM403 agent_grant_escalationTool, command and path rulesRuntime, inside the computerAsk waits, deny refusesConnector rulesConnector broker202 held, 403 deniedNo connector calls to private addressesConnector brokerconnector_egress_blockedEnforced secret, listed hosts onlySecret brokerNot swappedPush only to its own branchKortix git403Merge needs project.gitops.mergeKortix API403 CR_SELF_MERGE_REFUSEDRun it where your policy says.And read every line of what you run.Kortix CloudWe run the control plane and the computers.Self-hostedThe app, API and database on your server.Your VPC or on-premA single-tenant deployment, scoped with us.Open sourceRead it, fork it, audit it.SAML 2.0 and SCIM 2.0Your identity provider decides who gets in.Any modelYour own provider keys, or Kortix-managed.SOC 2Type IVerifiedSOC 2 Type I verifiedGDPR operated. We hold no other certification and imply none.Bring us your reviewSecurity questions.Answered from the code.Anything else, write to the team.{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How does an agent authenticate to Kortix?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each session computer gets KORTIX_TOKEN. It acts as that session’s agent, limited to its project, and ends with the session. It holds the agent’s permissions, never the role of the person who started it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which API keys and tokens exist?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every credential names its kind in its prefix: kortix_pat_ acts as you, kortix_sa_ as a service account, kortix_oat_ as a person who approved an app for 1 hour, kortix_gw_ reaches only the LLM gateway, and kortix_scim_ only directory sync. A missing or invalid token gets 401. A valid one without the permission gets 403."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an agent read our connector logins?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Kortix stores the login and makes each call itself. The login never enters the session’s computer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can code in a session read a secret?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A secret delivered as an environment variable is a real value, so code in the session can read it. Mark a web API key Enforced and the computer gets a stand-in instead. Kortix swaps in the real value outside the computer, only on requests to the hosts you list, and an echoed value comes back as [REDACTED]."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Kortix filter outbound network traffic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not today. A computer can reach the internet directly, for example to install packages. What Kortix enforces: enforced secrets go only to listed hosts, connector calls never reach private addresses, and a copied session token gets no enforced secret outside its own computer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can approve a held action?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A project manager, or the person who started the session. An approval covers one exact call. A held call expires after 24 hours unless the project sets another time, from 5 minutes to 30 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an agent merge its own changes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only with the project.gitops.merge permission. Without it, the merge answers 403. The built-in kortix agent holds every Kortix permission, so remove the merge permission from it to require a person every time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the audit log record, and can we export it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Who did what, when, how they signed in, and whether it was allowed, refusals included. When an agent acts, the row names the person it acted for. Events stay readable for 90 days and sit in a locked archive to day 365. Reading, exporting and streaming the log is an Enterprise feature."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do the models keep our data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kortix-managed models run only through inference providers with zero data retention. With your own provider key, your agreement with that provider applies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where does a self-hosted Kortix run sessions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The web app, API and database run on your server. Sessions still run on Platinum cloud computers, which call back to your server, so it must be reachable from the internet."}}]}How does an agent authenticate to Kortix?Each session computer gets KORTIX_TOKEN. It acts as that session’s agent, limited to its project, and ends with the session. It holds the agent’s permissions, never the role of the person who started it.Which API keys and tokens exist?Every credential names its kind in its prefix: kortix_pat_ acts as you, kortix_sa_ as a service account, kortix_oat_ as a person who approved an app for 1 hour, kortix_gw_ reaches only the LLM gateway, and kortix_scim_ only directory sync. A missing or invalid token gets 401. A valid one without the permission gets 403.Can an agent read our connector logins?No. Kortix stores the login and makes each call itself. The login never enters the session’s computer.Can code in a session read a secret?A secret delivered as an environment variable is a real value, so code in the session can read it. Mark a web API key Enforced and the computer gets a stand-in instead. Kortix swaps in the real value outside the computer, only on requests to the hosts you list, and an echoed value comes back as [REDACTED].Does Kortix filter outbound network traffic?Not today. A computer can reach the internet directly, for example to install packages. What Kortix enforces: enforced secrets go only to listed hosts, connector calls never reach private addresses, and a copied session token gets no enforced secret outside its own computer.Who can approve a held action?A project manager, or the person who started the session. An approval covers one exact call. A held call expires after 24 hours unless the project sets another time, from 5 minutes to 30 days.Can an agent merge its own changes?Only with the project.gitops.merge permission. Without it, the merge answers 403. The built-in kortix agent holds every Kortix permission, so remove the merge permission from it to require a person every time.What does the audit log record, and can we export it?Who did what, when, how they signed in, and whether it was allowed, refusals included. When an agent acts, the row names the person it acted for. Events stay readable for 90 days and sit in a locked archive to day 365. Reading, exporting and streaming the log is an Enterprise feature.Do the models keep our data?Kortix-managed models run only through inference providers with zero data retention. With your own provider key, your agreement with that provider applies.Where does a self-hosted Kortix run sessions?The web app, API and database run on your server. Sessions still run on Platinum cloud computers, which call back to your server, so it must be reachable from the internet.",
  "visuals": [
    [
      null,
      null,
      "SOC 2 Type I Verified",
    ],
  ],
}
`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition enterprise renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">From the first team to the whole company.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How Kortix works for a company" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-rollout" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Roll out team by team</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Start with one team. Add the next.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-infra" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Your infrastructure</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Kortix Cloud, your VPC or on-prem.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-models" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Models and spend control</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Any model, with limits you set.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-governance" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Governance in one place</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Sign-in, roles, approvals and audit.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-build" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Build on it</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">API, CLI, SDK and UI kit.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-work" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Working with us</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">A demo, a contract, a team behind it.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="topic-panel" aria-labelledby="topic-tab-rollout" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">Roll out team by team</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Each agent has a job, its skills and the connectors it may use. Grant each team its project and the agents it may run.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Drive gives people and agents shared folders. The company’s memory lives there as Markdown files every project member can read.</p></div><div class="bg-background flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-lg border"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b px-4 py-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span></span><span class="text-muted-foreground min-w-0 truncate font-mono text-xs">Arcadia · Drive</span></div><ul class="flex flex-col divide-y"><li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Company/Memory/</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">every project member</span></li><li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Company/Memory/customers.md</code></li><li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Company/Memory/conventions.md</code></li><li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Support/</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">shared with the Support group</span></li><li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">My files/</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">only you</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition compliance renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">One topic at a time.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How the controls work" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-identity" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Single sign-on and directory sync</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Your identity provider decides who gets in.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-access" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Roles, groups and agents</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Who opens which project, and runs which agent.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-governance" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Approvals and policy</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Rules in kortix.yaml, reviewed like code.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-audit" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Audit log</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Read it, export it, stream it.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="topic-panel" aria-labelledby="topic-tab-identity" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">Single sign-on and directory sync</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">People sign in with SAML 2.0 single sign-on. Enforce it, and other ways to sign in for your domain stop working.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">SCIM 2.0 keeps members and groups in sync. Map an identity provider group to a Kortix group once.</p></div><div class="bg-background flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-lg border"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b px-4 py-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span><span class="bg-muted-foreground/40 size-2.5 rounded-full"></span></span><span class="text-muted-foreground min-w-0 truncate font-mono text-xs">Identity → Group mappings</span></div><ul class="flex flex-col divide-y"><li class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-2.5"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase flex-1">Directory group</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="w-4"></span><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase flex-1">Kortix group</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-muted-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 font-mono text-xs break-all sm:text-sm">arcadia-eng</code><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="text-muted-foreground size-4 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z"></path></svg><span class="text-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm font-medium">Engineering</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-muted-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 font-mono text-xs break-all sm:text-sm">arcadia-support</code><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="text-muted-foreground size-4 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z"></path></svg><span class="text-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm font-medium">Support</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3"><code class="text-muted-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 font-mono text-xs break-all sm:text-sm">arcadia-fin</code><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="text-muted-foreground size-4 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z"></path></svg><span class="text-foreground min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm font-medium">Finance</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition sovereign renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">What runs where, and what you control.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How sovereign Kortix works" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-where" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">What runs where</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Your server, or Kortix Cloud.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-install" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Self-host with one CLI</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">One Docker Compose stack.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-updates" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Updates on your terms</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Daily, or pin a version.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-models" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Any model, set where you need it</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Your keys, your plan, your endpoint.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-files" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Your company is a repository</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Clone it, download it, keep it.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="topic-tab-secrets" aria-controls="topic-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Secret values stay out of git</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Names in the repo, values encrypted.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="topic-panel" aria-labelledby="topic-tab-where" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">What runs where</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Self-hosting puts the web app, the API, the LLM gateway and the database on your server.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Sessions and Drive still run on Platinum sandboxes. They call back to your instance, so it must be reachable from the internet.</p></div><table class="bg-background w-full table-fixed border-separate border-spacing-0 rounded-lg border text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">What runs where</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="w-5/12 border-b p-3 font-normal"><span class="sr-only">Part</span></th><th scope="col" class="border-b p-3 font-normal text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Kortix Cloud</th><th scope="col" class="border-b p-3 font-normal text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Self-hosted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium border-b">Web app, API, LLM gateway</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Kortix</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Your server</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium border-b">Database and file storage</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Kortix</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Your server</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium border-b">Accounts, secrets, audit log</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Kortix</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Your server</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium border-b">Sessions</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Platinum</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Platinum</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium border-b">Drive</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Platinum</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top border-b">Platinum</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="text-foreground p-3 align-top font-medium ">Models</th><td class="text-muted-foreground p-3 align-top ">Managed or yours</td><td class="text-foreground p-3 align-top ">Yours</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition self-hosted renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How self-hosting works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">From the first command to the daily update.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How self-hosting works" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-where" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">What runs where</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Your server, and Platinum.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-reach" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Reachability</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">A domain, or a tunnel to evaluate.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-setup" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">First sign-in</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Six steps in the web app.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-updates" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Updates and versions</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Daily, or pinned.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-enterprise" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Enterprise on your server</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">One flag, every account.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="selfhost-tab-needs" aria-controls="selfhost-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Requirements</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">What the server needs.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="selfhost-panel" aria-labelledby="selfhost-tab-where" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">What runs where</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">init writes one Docker Compose project. Every service in it runs on your server.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Sessions and Drive run on Platinum sandboxes. They call back to your instance.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-6"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Your server</span><ul class="bg-background flex flex-col divide-y rounded-lg border"><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">frontend</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">The web app</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">kortix-api</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">The REST API</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">llm-gateway</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">The LLM gateway</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">supabase-*</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">Postgres, auth and file storage</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">kortix-updater</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">Pulls, migrates and rolls daily</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">caddy</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">TLS on 80 and 443, domain mode</span></li></ul></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Platinum</span><ul class="bg-background flex flex-col divide-y rounded-lg border"><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Sessions</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">One sandbox per session</span></li><li class="flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6"><code class="text-foreground font-mono text-sm">Drive</code><span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm text-pretty sm:text-right">Platinum volumes</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition framework renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">One part at a time.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How the Kortix framework works" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-agents" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Agents</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">One block in kortix.yaml and one prompt file.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-extensions" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">pi extensions</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Extend the harness with TypeScript.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-rules" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Rules</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Allow, Ask or Block, per tool and per app call.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-triggers" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Triggers, 24/7</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">A schedule or a webhook starts the agent.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-computer" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">A computer per session</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">pi runs the agent on its own cloud computer.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-review" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Changes through review</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Work reaches main through a change request.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="framework-tab-build" aria-controls="framework-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Build your own experience</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">@kortix/sdk and @kortix/ui on the same backend.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="framework-panel" aria-labelledby="framework-tab-agents" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">Agents</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">An agent is a block in kortix.yaml and a Markdown prompt. The block names its model, tools, connectors and skills.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Access is deny-by-default. An agent gets no connector, secret or skill the block does not list.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><div class="bg-background flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-lg border"><p class="text-muted-foreground border-b px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">kortix.yaml</p><pre class="text-foreground overflow-x-auto px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-6"><code><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">  # Marketing</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">  </span><span class="text-foreground">marketing</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">description</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span> <span class="text-kortix-green">Drafts LinkedIn posts from shipped work.</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">prompt_file</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span> <span class="text-kortix-green">agents/marketing/content.md</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">tools</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span><span class="text-muted-foreground"> [read, web_search]</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">connectors</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span><span class="text-muted-foreground"> [linkedin, kortix_slack]</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">skills</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span><span class="text-muted-foreground"> [write-post]</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">commands</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span><span class="text-muted-foreground"> [draft-post]</span></span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre"><span class="text-muted-foreground">    </span><span class="text-foreground">extensions</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">:</span><span class="text-muted-foreground"> [web-access]</span></span></code></pre></div><div class="bg-background flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-lg border"><p class="text-muted-foreground border-b px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">agents/marketing/content.md</p><pre class="text-foreground overflow-x-auto px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-6"><code><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre">You write Arcadia LinkedIn posts from work the team shipped.</span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre">Follow the write-post skill and the tone in the company memory.</span><span class="block leading-6 break-words whitespace-pre-wrap lg:min-w-max lg:whitespace-pre">Every post waits for a person to approve it.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition multiplayer renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">From one person to the whole team.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="How multiplayer works" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-share" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Share a session</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Private by default. The owner opens it up.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-together" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Work in it together</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Everyone with access reads it and continues it.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-channels" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Slack and Microsoft Teams</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Mention the bot. The agent replies in the thread.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-access" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Who may run which agent</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Roles per account and project, agents per person.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-approve" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">People approve</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">You decide what an agent does without a person.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="team-tab-personal" aria-controls="team-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Personal stays personal</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Your own accounts reach only your private sessions.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="team-panel" aria-labelledby="team-tab-share" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">Share a session</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">A session is private to the person who started it. The owner can open it to chosen people and groups, or to the whole project.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">A public link shows it read-only to anyone with the link. Revoke it at any time.</p></div><div class="bg-background flex flex-col rounded-lg border"><ul class="flex flex-col divide-y"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-0.5 flex size-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border"></span><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1"><p class="text-foreground text-base">Only you</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">The owner. This is the default.</p></div></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-0.5 flex size-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-foreground"><span class="bg-foreground size-2 rounded-full"></span></span><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1"><p class="text-foreground text-base font-medium">Specific people</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">The owner, plus the members and groups they pick.</p><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 pt-1.5"><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">Member 2</li><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">Finance</li></ul></div></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-0.5 flex size-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border"></span><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1"><p class="text-foreground text-base">Whole project</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Every member of the project.</p></div></li></ul><p class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-2 border-t p-4 text-sm"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="size-4 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M165.66,90.34a8,8,0,0,1,0,11.32l-64,64a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32l64-64A8,8,0,0,1,165.66,90.34ZM215.6,40.4a56,56,0,0,0-79.2,0L106.34,70.45a8,8,0,0,0,11.32,11.32l30.06-30a40,40,0,0,1,56.57,56.56l-30.07,30.06a8,8,0,0,0,11.31,11.32L215.6,119.6a56,56,0,0,0,0-79.2ZM138.34,174.22l-30.06,30.06a40,40,0,1,1-56.56-56.57l30.05-30.05a8,8,0,0,0-11.32-11.32L40.4,136.4a56,56,0,0,0,79.2,79.2l30.06-30.07a8,8,0,0,0-11.32-11.31Z"></path></svg>Public link: read-only, no sign-in.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;

exports[`shipped marketing route composition security renders its topic tabs section unchanged 1`] = `"<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-16 py-14 lg:py-20"><div class="kx-rail-fade relative border-y px-4 lg:px-17"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="px-4 py-12 lg:px-11 lg:py-16 lg:pr-12"><h2 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">How it works.<span class="text-muted-foreground block">One layer at a time.</span></h2><div role="tablist" aria-label="Layers of the security model" aria-orientation="vertical" class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6"><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-identity" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Identity and roles</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Who may open a project, and which agents they may run.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-agent" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Agent permissions</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">An agent acts as itself, with only what you grant.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-computer" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">The computer and egress</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Each session gets its own isolated cloud computer.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-connectors" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Connectors and approvals</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Kortix holds the login and decides each call.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-secrets" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Secrets</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Encrypted per project, delivered only where allowed.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-models" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Models</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Every model request passes one gateway.</p></button><button type="button" role="tab" id="layer-tab-changes" aria-controls="layer-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="outline-ring duration-moderate w-full rounded-sm text-left opacity-50 transition-opacity ease-out hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 aria-selected:opacity-100"><h3 class="text-foreground text-base font-medium text-pretty">Changes and review</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm text-balance">Work reaches main through a change request.</p></button></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="layer-panel" aria-labelledby="layer-tab-identity" class="bg-card flex items-center justify-center border-t p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:p-12"><div class="animate-in fade-in duration-slower flex w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex-col gap-8 ease-out"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><h3 class="text-foreground text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">Identity and roles</h3><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">People sign in with SAML single sign-on, or a password with two-factor.</p><p class="text-muted-foreground text-base text-pretty">Each person holds an account role and a role in each project. Groups grant a project to many people at once.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-6"><div class="flex flex-col gap-2"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Account role</span><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-base">Owner</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" aria-hidden="true" class="text-muted-foreground size-3.5"><path d="M181.66,133.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L164.69,128,90.34,53.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l80,80A8,8,0,0,1,181.66,133.66Z"></path></svg></li><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-base">Admin</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" aria-hidden="true" class="text-muted-foreground size-3.5"><path d="M181.66,133.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L164.69,128,90.34,53.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l80,80A8,8,0,0,1,181.66,133.66Z"></path></svg></li><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-base">Member</span></li></ol></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Project role</span><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-base">Manager</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" aria-hidden="true" class="text-muted-foreground size-3.5"><path d="M181.66,133.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L164.69,128,90.34,53.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l80,80A8,8,0,0,1,181.66,133.66Z"></path></svg></li><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-base">Member</span></li></ol></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2"><span class="text-muted-foreground font-mono text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">Sign-in</span><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">SAML 2.0 SSO</li><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">SCIM 2.0</li><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">Two-factor</li><li class="bg-muted text-foreground rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 text-sm">Session timeout</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>"`;
